`format_to_regex(fmt)` has no mutable external state and uses only deterministic operations on the provided `fmt`: one `re.search`, one `re.finditer` loop, `re.escape`, string concatenation, and integer/string cursor updates. With the fixed test input `'%(title)s - %(artist)s [%(album)s].%(ext)s'`, the first condition `if not re.search(...)` always evaluates the same way, the `for match in re.finditer(...)` loop finds the same four placeholders in the same order on every call, and the trailing `if lastpos < len(fmt)` check also evaluates the same way each time. Since no branch depends on anything that changes between calls, all five invocations execute the same sequence of lines, so there is exactly one distinct path.

